          {
            "x": 2.23463687150838,
            "y": 13.245033112582783,
            "width": 92.73743016759778,
            "height": 86.09271523178808,
            "action": {
              "library": "H5P.AdvancedText 1.1",
              "params": {
                "text": "<p><strong>George Orwell's Early Life</strong><br>\nEric Arthur Blair, known by his pen name George Orwell, was born in 1903 in Motihari, India, where his father worked in the opium department of the Indian Civil Service. Orwell's early years were marked by a sense of displacement, which he reflected upon in his later writing. His family moved back to England, and he was sent to a boarding school that inspired a lifelong aversion to authority figures and provided material for his first book, \"Down and Out in Paris and London.\"</p>\n\n<p><strong>Education and Imperial Service</strong><br>\nOrwell's education at Eton on a scholarship was significant as it shaped his writing and political views. Despite his intellect, he did not pursue university education. Instead, he joined the Indian Imperial Police in Burma. His five years in service deeply affected his views on imperialism and social justice, leading to his eventual resignation and decision to become a writer.</p>\n\n<p><strong>Writing Career Beginnings</strong><br>\nAfter leaving Burma, Orwell struggled with poverty and took various low-paying jobs. He used these experiences to explore social injustice, which became a recurring theme in his work. His firsthand experiences with the underclass provided the material for his early writings. Orwell's time in Paris and London was a period of hardship but also crucial in forging his identity as a writer who champions the voiceless.</p>\n"
              },
              "metadata": {
                "contentType": "Text",
                "license": "U",
                "title": "Unbenannt: Text",
                "defaultLanguage": "en"
              },
              "subContentId": "53bc5361-5ce5-43a9-a00f-57bbceee9cd0"
            },
            "alwaysDisplayComments": false,
            "backgroundOpacity": 0,
            "displayAsButton": false,
